From 2fbc15ea7f02247c6eae1398d7508ca33ff08132 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <claude@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 29 Jul 2026 19:06:40 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Mortgage cassette: first cassette enabling outcome_obligation

First real cassette to enable the outcome_obligation capability
(cassette_capabilities.OutcomeObligations), first real test of the
capability/hashed-field/twin-derivation separation outside the IVR
reference domain.

- CAPABILITIES = (CAPABILITY_OUTCOME_OBLIGATION,) only -- kernel-only
  otherwise, no call-center surface (matches banking's precedent of
  honestly declaring an absent capability).
- get_maturation_rule() -> loan_performance@3y (1095 days). Replaces
  the roadmap's original 24-month default, which doesn't fit
  mortgages. Researched replacement: the mortgage industry's own
  3-year 'seasoning' convention (Urban Institute / Dallas Fed
  mortgage-default research; FDIC: 43% of eventual defaulters have
  defaulted by year 3, vs 10% by year 1). validate() self-checks that
  this and the outcome_horizon_days governance parameter cannot
  silently diverge.
- classify_outcome(evidence): resolution_type paid_in_full -> True,
  involuntary_closure -> False (foreclosure/short_sale/deed_in_lieu
  stay one bucket; the mechanism sub-detail never changes the
  verdict), anything else -> None (genuinely ambiguous, not guessed).
- judge()/explain(): decision-process-integrity scoring -- penalizes
  requested-vs-actual mismatches and outcome reasons too thin
  (< 3 words) to be a documented basis for an adverse action.
  Deliberately lighter-weight than regulatory_checks' Reg B
  boilerplate-phrase screening, which stays a separate opt-in lens.
- PROPERTY_ADDRESS_FIELD = 'loan_property_address': no prior
  input_fields convention existed anywhere in the real repo for a
  property address (input_fields is a free-form Dict[str, Any] per
  cassette); this is the field the property-address geocoding for the
  planned regional-equity cohort dimension will read.

Left open, not this commit: the ABANDON-on-modification orchestration
(a permanent loan modification issuing a new loan number supersedes
the original obligation) is documented in the module docstring but
belongs at the obligation_sweep.py orchestration layer, not cassette
logic. The ZIP/county regional-equity cohort dimension itself is also
not built here -- this commit is the cassette only.

27 new tests. Full suite 629 passed / 6 skipped, twice back-to-back
(602 prior baseline + 27 new).
